{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310832,"nonce":"gyoqQPnHC0ry0lMejIM1mwRTQO4=","title":"LANDED 7f48c1ae + 145cd55d (2026-09-12): Dynamic = box everywhere, readers dispatch on the TAG; arrays box as TYPE_ARRAY; E0801 is a ...","message":"**THE CONVENTION, now enforced in one direction:** a Dynamic slot holds a\n`DynamicValue` box, and a reader that must know what it holds reads the\nTAG (`haxe_dynamic_field`, `haxe_dynamic_tag`, `haxe_unbox_if_tag`,\n`haxe_iter_handle_from_dynamic` in runtime/src). What made it hold:\n- `runtime_type_id(Array)` = 7 (TYPE_ARRAY) and the `Array` class symbol\n  maps to 7 too, so `Std.isOfType(d, Array)` and `cast(d, Array)` agree\n  with the box (mir/helpers/type_ids.rs).\n- `return \u003cconcrete\u003e` into a Dynamic return type BOXES (statements.rs) --\n  it came back raw before, and `v.length` on it read the array header.\n- Dynamic -\u003e Array/String/Anonymous unbox through `haxe_unbox_if_tag`:\n  SAFE because those raw objects begin with a DATA POINTER, never the tag.\n  A class box vs a raw class instance is NOT distinguishable (both start\n  with the class id) -- that ambiguity remains, by convention only.\n- The E0801 \"ambiguous dynamic dispatch\" site is a runtime SWITCH on the\n  tag among the candidates (mir/helpers/dynamic_dispatch.rs); every\n  name-resolved stdlib call on a Dynamic receiver unboxes the receiver\n  (`unbox_dynamic_receiver`) -- there were FIVE such emission sites\n  (stdlib_instance unique/wrapper/mono-var, stdlib_runtime x4,\n  extern_class), found one at a time by `RAYZOR_TRACE_STDLIB_DISPATCH=1`.\n- Results through a Dynamic receiver are boxed by the mapping's declared\n  return (`box_dispatch_result`); registered in `boxed_value_regs` or the\n  Let marks the register as a RAW ANON HANDLE (raw_anon_symbols) and\n  reflection reads the box as the object.\n- Runtime-backed classes (ArrayIterator, the maps) are REGISTERED with the\n  mapping's method names (`register_stdlib_runtime_class_rtti`), so\n  `it.hasNext == null` is false on a boxed iterator; `Reflect.field` of a\n  declared METHOD is a TYPE_FUNCTION box (non-null, isFunction true, not\n  callable).\n\n**FOUND ON THE WAY, worse than the target:** `try { return X; }` lost X for\nEVERY type (Int -\u003e 0, String -\u003e \"\", Bool -\u003e false): the try's exit branch\nREPLACED the body's return terminator (set_terminator overwrites). Fix\n145cd55d: `try_depth` on the context, a return pops that many handlers,\nthe try leaves a terminated body alone, an unreachable continuation when\nevery path left. TRAP: `set_terminator` silently overwrites -- any lowering\nthat appends an exit after `lower_block` must check `is_terminated()`.\n\n**STILL OPEN (a957716):** a Dynamic ITERATION yields the array's raw i64\nelements under a Dynamic type -- 0 prints as null, a String element as\n`\u003cunknown type\u003e` (Issue9372, Issue5293). HaxeArray carries NO element\nkind. Also Issue5477: `function add(x) { hash[0] = x; }` -- an untyped\nparam is not inferred from an INDEX store (only `this.f = p` and calls).\n\nMEASURED: 522 -\u003e 533, LOST 0, 11 GAINED, every other MOVED row is\nCRASH -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER; suite 207/0/1; fixtures 18/18 (RuntimeMetadata\nstarted passing on its own -- it was the return-inside-try bug).\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): LANDED 7f48c1ae+145cd55d: Dynamic = BOX, readers dispatch on the TAG (arrays box as 7; E0801 = runtime tag switch; 5 receiver-unbox sites). `try { return X }` lost X for EVERY type (set_terminator overwrites). 522-\u003e533. OPEN: raw elements yielded from a Dynamic array (a957716).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_dynamic_is_a_box_landed` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}